Z||000000||fieroX||11-07-2001||05:09 AM||||as some of you know I lowered my car the other day, (sorry I dont have any pics yet) but anyway I noticed afterward that under acceleration between 20 and 35 mph there is a slight vibration.  any above 35 and its gone, totally smooth, under 20 totally smooth, I cant pinpoint it.  So I took my car in and had a 4 wheel alignment done on it today, the car handles awesome.  the wheels are perfectly straight (and better be for $85), but I still have that vibration.  does anybody else with a lowered car have some sort of vibration that occured after lowering?  what could it be?  thanks<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||11-07-2001||08:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>as some of you know I lowered my car the other day, (sorry I dont have any pics yet) but anyway I noticed afterward that under acceleration between 20 and 35 mph there is a slight vibration.  any above 35 and its gone, totally smooth, under 20 totally smooth, I cant pinpoint it.  So I took my car in and had a 4 wheel alignment done on it today, the car handles awesome.  the wheels are perfectly straight (and better be for $85), but I still have that vibration.  does anybody else with a lowered car have some sort of vibration that occured after lowering?  what could it be?  thanks<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How much did you lower it, and HOW did you lower it?<BR>If you cut or sagged the springs, good luck...<BR>By dropping the SPRING height, you change the geometry of the suspention...<BR>Also, how old are the suspention components?<BR>Rotted rubber bushings, worn out ball joints, and loose wheel bearings could all cause problems...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroX||11-07-2001||01:47 PM||||I took out 1.5 coils in the rear, and 1.6 coils in the front.  Which put it down about 1.5 inches all around.  The suspension is most likely original, but will be replaced when I undergo completion of my engine swap.   I wonder now if its my engine causing the vibration, like a misfire or something.  I just remembered that yesterday when I first fired it up, it shook like that at idle for about 8 seconds and then smoothed out. So I dont think its in the driveline if its doing it at idle.  The engine has 152,000 on it so its about time to splode.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||11-07-2001||02:01 PM||||The half shafts can also cause a vibration. I know you can buy axle stabilizers but don't know how well they work. I changed out the half shafts on my car and got rid of the vibration problems I had. Could have been a C V joint was going bad too.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-07-2001||02:59 PM||||did you cut out enough thats its sitting on the bumpstops? that would transfer lots of vibration.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||11-07-2001||06:22 PM||||It is most likely something in one of the drive axles that is now more pronounced with changed suspension geometry.  Any vibration caused by acceleration is usually drivetrain related.  Alex4mula also had the same thing happen when he lowered his 3nd car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fieroX||11-10-2001||02:06 PM||||I dont believe it is in the drive train or suspension.  I think now that it is some rotating force on the engine.  The vibration increases in force with rpm, and sometimes does it while in park.  Im thinking its the harmonic balancer.  But now I dont care.  I just need it to last 2 more months, and bye bye 2.8 and hello 3800.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||11-10-2001||02:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>I dont believe it is in the drive train or suspension.  I think now that it is some rotating force on the engine.  The vibration increases in force with rpm, and sometimes does it while in park.  Im thinking its the harmonic balancer.  But now I dont care.  I just need it to last 2 more months, and bye bye 2.8 and hello 3800.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like you are either missing, or a major bearing is on it's way out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||3
